[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Spice V2 - Development Standards and Tiered Verification

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Version 2.0, 2026-11-20. Adapts the user's standing development standards (DEV-*) cleanly for the Spice V2 C++20 + .NET architecture, preserving honest coverage, meaningful comments, StrictDoc traceability, and adversarial testing while adding explicit verification tiers and anti-bloat guardrails so engineering velocity stays high.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1. Languages, tooling and documentation discipline

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-LANG-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: C++20 core with C#/F# host and automation
STATEMENT: >>>
The core simulation engine shall be implemented in C++20 with CMake and vcpkg; C# and F# shall be used for the host SDK, StarLark-cs integration, schematic UI, and automation scripts by default, with PowerShell cmdlets on Windows and standard shell tooling in Linux CI where PowerShell is absent.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Inspect CMakeLists.txt, vcpkg.json, and v2/dotnet projects.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-TOOL-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Native and managed test frameworks
STATEMENT: >>>
C++20 tests shall execute via CTest (preferring Catch2 via vcpkg, with a zero-dependency standalone harness fallback for offline environments); .NET tests shall use xUnit and FsCheck for property-based testing; PowerShell scripts shall use Pester where applicable.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Run ctest and dotnet test and preserve execution summaries.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-TOOL-004
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Columnar data interchange
STATEMENT: >>>
Apache Arrow shall be preferred for high-throughput columnar waveform interchange between native and managed layers, with HDF5/RAW/CSV/VCD/Touchstone supported per ARCH-CAP-005.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Verify schema round-trips on real and complex simulation waveforms.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-DOC-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Meaningful synchronized comments
STATEMENT: >>>
Public interfaces, units, sign conventions, handle ownership, numerical assumptions, and non-obvious invariants shall be commented meaningfully and updated alongside code changes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Review changed headers and implementation files for accurate interface and numerical comments.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-DOC-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Six-file authoritative StrictDoc set (anti-sprawl)
STATEMENT: >>>
Authoritative V2 software requirements shall live in StrictDoc under v2/docs/requirements/ in a bounded set of six domain documents (architecture, capabilities, schematic, physical-audits, implementation-plan, development-standards) with stable unique UIDs and honest statuses. One-off .sdoc files shall not be created per bugfix, PR, or mutant replay.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Validate UID uniqueness, parent link resolution, and document count under v2/docs/requirements/.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 2. Coverage, tiered verification and GPU discipline

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-COV-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Honest scoped coverage reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
Code changes shall report actual line and branch coverage where supported (gcov/llvm-cov for C++20, Coverlet for C#), explicitly separating owned code from third-party/vendor libraries and reporting any unmeasured scopes or unavailable tooling honestly without inventing metrics.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Inspect tool output and reported line/branch counts, exclusions, and missing-tool disclosures.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-TEST-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Malformed inputs and boundary testing
STATEMENT: >>>
Every public boundary (C ABI, IR validation, parsers, OSDI loader, schematic ERC) shall test null/stale handles, mismatched versions, malformed syntax, nonfinite numbers, and resource limits with explicit fail-closed diagnostics.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Execute negative boundary suites in Tier 1 CTest and xUnit runs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-TEST-006
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Reproducible seeds and regression retention
STATEMENT: >>>
Randomized, property-based, and fuzz tests shall record seeds, minimized counterexamples, and replay commands; confirmed defects shall become permanent deterministic Tier 1 regressions.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Replay retained seeds and verify regressions fail against unpatched code.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-TEST-009
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Three-tier verification cadence
STATEMENT: >>>
Verification shall operate in three bounded tiers so quality stays high without stalling feature delivery: Tier 1 (every commit, target under 60 seconds: unit, negative-boundary, opt-in physical audits, and fast differential smoke); Tier 2 (PR and milestone: curated Xyce/ngspice oracle suite, property tests, and scoped line/branch coverage); Tier 3 (scheduled or release gate: targeted mutation testing on numerical/audit kernels and bounded parser/ABI fuzzing).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Confirm Tier 1 remains fast enough for every commit and Tier 3 campaigns never block routine feature merges.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-GPU-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Evidence-gated GPU adoption
STATEMENT: >>>
GPU dependencies and mandatory GPU test gates shall not be introduced until the CPU C++20 + KLU engine is qualified and transfer-inclusive benchmarks on 1,000+ unknown circuits demonstrate clear end-to-end speedup; a qualified CPU path shall always remain primary.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Inspect CMake and CI configuration to confirm zero mandatory GPU gates before M4b benchmarks justify them.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DEV-REPORT-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Honest concise delivery reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
Delivery updates shall report what changed, what actually ran, measured coverage/benchmark results, and explicit limitations without claiming unexecuted checks passed.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Cross-check delivery summaries against actual command outputs.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
